+For the half-space Stokes first-problem model, choose $\nu=1\,\mathrm{m^2\,s^{-1}}$, $U=1\,\mathrm{m\,s^{-1}}$, and $t=1\,\mathrm s$. At $y=2\sqrt{\log2}\,\mathrm m$, the exact Gaussian-tail estimate gives $|u|\le\tfrac12\,\mathrm{m\,s^{-1}}$. For the separate torus shear choose $\nu=1\,\mathrm{m^2\,s^{-1}}$, $L_x=L_y=L_z=2\pi\,\mathrm m$, $m=1$, $k=1\,\mathrm{m^{-1}}$, $A=2\,\mathrm{m\,s^{-1}}$, $b=\pi/3\,\mathrm m$, and $c=1\,\mathrm m$. Then $\alpha=\pi/3$ and
 $$\Gamma(t)=2C_{\pi/3}e^{-t/(1\,\mathrm s)}\,\mathrm{m^2\,s^{-1}},\qquad C_{\pi/3}=\int_0^{2\pi}\cos\theta\sin((\pi/3)\cos\theta)\,d\theta>0.$$
 These are exact model values, not measured velocity or circulation.
 
